IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `imm-types`
IMPORT `imm-status`

-- Immigration Act 2009 — GOAL 3: DEPORTATION LIABILITY.
--
--   "Is a residence class visa holder liable for deportation for offending;
--    until when; and by when must the person respond or appeal?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2009_51.txt — ss 157, 161,
-- 167.

§ `Goal 3 — deportation liability`

-- s 161 "(3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a)(iii), (b), (c), and (d),
-- the periods of 2 years, 5 years, and 10 years after a person first held a
-- residence class visa are to be determined exclusive of any time spent by
-- the person in imprisonment following conviction for any offence." The days
-- imprisoned extend the period (fork F2).
@ref s 161(3)
GIVEN span IS A NUMBER, r IS A `Resident facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the` span `year period after first holding a residence class visa, facts` r MEANS
    `the day` (r's `days imprisoned since first holding the visa`) `days after` (`add years` (r's `first held a residence class visa on`) span)

-- s 161 "(1) A residence class visa holder is liable for deportation if they
-- are convicted ... of,— (a) an offence for which the court has the power to
-- impose imprisonment for a term of 3 months or more if the offence was
-- committed at any time— (i) when the person was unlawfully in New Zealand;
-- or (ii) when the person held a temporary entry class visa; or (iii) not
-- later than 2 years after the person first held a residence class visa; or
-- (b) an offence for which the court has the power to impose imprisonment for
-- a term of 2 years or more, if the offence was committed not later than 5
-- years after the person first held a residence class visa; or (c) an offence
-- and sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 5 years or more ..., if the
-- offence was committed not later than 10 years after ...; or (d) an offence
-- against section 350(1), 351, or 351A, if the offence was committed not
-- later than 10 years after the person first held a residence class visa".
@ref s 161(1), (3)
GIVEN r IS A `Resident facts`, c IS A Conviction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction makes the resident liable for deportation` r c IF
        (    c's `maximum imprisonment available, in years` AT LEAST 0.25
         AND (   c's `committed while unlawfully in New Zealand or on a temporary entry class visa`
              OR c's `offence committed on` AT MOST `the end of the` 2 `year period after first holding a residence class visa, facts` r))
    OR  (    c's `maximum imprisonment available, in years` AT LEAST 2
         AND c's `offence committed on` AT MOST `the end of the` 5 `year period after first holding a residence class visa, facts` r)
    OR  (    c's `sentence of imprisonment, in years` AT LEAST 5
         AND c's `offence committed on` AT MOST `the end of the` 10 `year period after first holding a residence class visa, facts` r)
    OR  (    c's `an offence against s 350(1), 351 or 351A`
         AND c's `offence committed on` AT MOST `the end of the` 10 `year period after first holding a residence class visa, facts` r)

@ref s 161(1)
@export Whether a residence class visa holder is liable for deportation for offending under s 161 of the Immigration Act 2009 (NZ): a conviction for an offence punishable by 3 months' imprisonment committed while unlawful, on a temporary visa, or within 2 years of first holding a residence class visa; by 2 years' imprisonment within 5 years; a sentence of 5 years or more within 10 years; or an employer offence under ss 350(1), 351 or 351A within 10 years — those periods not counting time in prison. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Resident facts`  @desc When the person first held a residence class visa, days imprisoned since, and their convictions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resident is liable for deportation under s 161` r IF
    any (GIVEN c YIELD `the conviction makes the resident liable for deportation` r c) (r's `resident convictions`)

-- s 167 "(1) Residence class visa holders remain liable for deportation for a
-- period of 10 years following the arising of the liability for deportation.
-- (2) The period of 10 years ... must be calculated exclusive of— (a) any time
-- spent by the person in imprisonment following conviction for any offence:
-- (b) any period of time when the person's liability for deportation is
-- suspended".
@ref s 167(1)-(2)
@export The last day a residence class visa holder remains liable for deportation under s 167 of the Immigration Act 2009 (NZ): 10 years after the liability arose, extended by time in prison and time the liability was suspended. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Liability period facts`  @desc When the liability arose, and the days imprisoned or suspended since
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of deportation liability, facts` l MEANS
    `the day` (l's `days imprisoned or suspended since`) `days after` (`add years` (l's `liability arose on`) 10)

-- s 157 "(2) The person has 14 days from the date of service of the
-- deportation liability notice to give good reason why deportation should not
-- proceed. ... (4) A temporary visa holder or interim visa holder who is
-- liable ... may, not later than 28 days after the date of service of a
-- deportation liability notice, appeal to the Tribunal". s 161 "(2) A person
-- liable for deportation under this section may, not later than 28 days after
-- being served with a deportation liability notice, appeal to the Tribunal".
@ref ss 157(2), (4), 161(2)
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give reasons against deportation, notice served` served MEANS
    `the day` 14 `days after` served

@ref ss 157(4), 161(2)
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to appeal a deportation liability notice served` served MEANS
    `the day` 28 `days after` served
